Honour the SNI option on QUIC links

linkQUIC.dial cloned the TLS config and set ServerName on the clone, then passed
the original l.tlsconfig to quic.DialAddr, so the clone was never used. The
sni= option (linkOptions.tlsSNI) was not read at all: a quic:// peer sent no
server name, because quic-go falls back to the dialled IP literal and crypto/tls
leaves an IP out of the ClientHello.

  dial passes the clone to DialAddr, as linkTLS does
  ServerName is the peer's host name, or sni= when given
  the MinVersion/MaxVersion lines on the clone are gone: they were dead code,
  and once the clone is used TLS 1.2 would undercut the base config (TLS 1.3)

link_quic_test.go reads the server name that a local QUIC listener receives.

diff --git a/src/core/link_quic.go b/src/core/link_quic.go
